# xippios-{{ source_slug }}

Typed Python client, MCP server and FastAPI routes for
[{{ source_name }}]({{ upstream_url }}), part of the
[xippios SDK family](https://github.com/xippios). Names and semantics follow the
upstream documentation; every response carries release metadata (source, endpoint,
retrieved_at, published_at, vintage).

## Install

```bash
uv add xippios-{{ source_slug }}            # client only
uv add "xippios-{{ source_slug }}[mcp]"     # + MCP server
uv add "xippios-{{ source_slug }}[http]"    # + FastAPI router
```

{% if api_key_env %}
Set `{{ api_key_env }}` in the environment. Nothing is read from files.
{% else %}
No API key is needed.
{% endif %}

## 30-second example

```python
from xippios.{{ source_pkg }} import tasks

# result = tasks.<task>(...)
# result.data, result.meta.retrieved_at, result.meta.request
```

Task functions are listed in the status table below as they are added.

## MCP

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "{{ source_slug }}": {
      "command": "uvx",
      "args": ["--from", "xippios-{{ source_slug }}[mcp]", "xippios-{{ source_slug }}-mcp"]{% if api_key_env %},
      "env": { "{{ api_key_env }}": "..." }
{% endif %}
    }
  }
}
```

Tools are read-only and named `{{ tool_prefix }}_<verb>_<noun>`. Results are capped at
200 rows or 64 KB with a note on how to narrow the query. `--http` serves streamable
HTTP instead of stdio.
{% if needs_write_tools %}

Write tools run in a separate server, `xippios-{{ source_slug }}-mcp-write`; every write
tool previews its change unless called with `confirm=true`.
{% endif %}

